comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T12:59:17.974Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: request-specific live search plus fresh open/in_progress lists and the complete3077-item corpus found only the completed parent for this newly reviewed composition gap. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1559#discussion_r4359748681. Reuse the existing SDK guard rather than add a second command classifier."
  "2026-10-23T13:01:49.125Z","harness:codex","Negative control: the unchanged candidate fails five regressions across the real CLI integration and public SDK recovery tests. The returned retries preserve non-executable assignment/comment commands instead of requesting an actual command. Reuse assertLinkedTestCommand on trimmed candidates in both structured and bare command branches; valid structured metadata remains in the command-required template."
  "2026-10-23T13:03:45.659Z","harness:codex","Final local verification:86 linked tests pass with a durable execution receipt. The five negative controls now receive command-required templates and no executable retry; valid structured metadata and literal bare-command bytes retain their previous recovery. Source/static quality,100 percent docstring gates, type checking, changed-file lint and generated SDK/error/capability checks pass. The completed free full review produced this single actionable finding, which is addressed by reusing the shared guard rather than extending a separate classifier."
